## Implementation Checklist

When generating user guides using this rule:

### File Organization
- [ ] Create `/guides` folder in project root
- [ ] Generate 6 files total (3 MD + 3 HTML for each user type)
- [ ] Use exact naming convention: `[user-type]-user-guide.[md|html]`

### Content Verification  
- [ ] Verify every feature exists in actual codebase before documenting
- [ ] Confirm all UI elements reference actual Angular components
- [ ] Validate all workflow steps against business logic code
- [ ] Check all permissions against Identity system code
- [ ] Ask for clarification when code is unclear rather than assume

### User-Specific Documentation
- [ ] **Anonymous users**: Only document guest application features
- [ ] **External users**: Only document external authenticated features  
- [ ] **Internal users**: Only document internal authenticated features
- [ ] Ensure no feature overlap between user types unless code confirms shared access

### End-User Focus
- [ ] Use non-technical language appropriate for system users
- [ ] Focus on user goals and outcomes, not technical implementation
- [ ] Provide step-by-step instructions based on actual UI flow
- [ ] Include troubleshooting for common user scenarios
- [ ] Reference actual button names, menus, and field labels from components

### Quality Assurance
- [ ] Validate all instructions can be followed by target users
- [ ] Ensure workflow diagrams reflect actual system behavior
- [ ] Include appropriate screenshot placeholders with exact locations
- [ ] Use consistent terminology throughout all guides
- [ ] Plan for maintenance when codebase changes

### HTML Styling Compliance
- [ ] Use 'Noto Sans' font family from Google Fonts
- [ ] Apply UNOPS color scheme (#005f88 primary, #00669a secondary)
- [ ] Implement responsive design for mobile compatibility
- [ ] Include proper heading hierarchy and semantic markup
- [ ] Ensure accessibility standards (WCAG compliance)

## Success Criteria

A successful user guide generated using this rule should:

1. **Enable End Users**: Allow people using the system to complete their tasks independently without technical knowledge
2. **Reflect Actual System**: Match 100% with actual system behavior and capabilities as implemented in code
3. **User-Type Specific**: Clearly separate functionality by user category (anonymous/external/internal)
4. **Stay Current**: Be maintainable and updateable as the codebase evolves
5. **Reduce Support**: Minimize user confusion and support requests through accurate, clear instructions
6. **File Organization**: Properly organized in `/guides` folder with correct naming conventions
7. **Content Verification**: Every documented feature verified to exist in actual codebase

